CORE
stime1.sv
--bound 1
^\[main\.p0\] always \$bits\(\$stime\(\)\) == 32: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p1\] always \$stime\(\) == 0: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
$stime type-checks (1800-2017 20.3.3), yielding a 32-bit unsigned
integer. As EBMC has no notion of continuous simulation time, the
value is nondeterministic, and hence the property fixing it to 0 is
refuted.
